      "instrument_id": "EQ21",
      "role": "primary",
      "technique": "Thermomechanical constrained-recovery testing via hybrid rheometry with temperature control",
      "why": "This rheometer has a confirmed Environmental Test Chamber (ETC) for precise thermal activation and can measure axial recovery force (within its normal-force transducer limit, typically up to ~50 N) or torsional recovery stress while holding strain constant. It is preferred over EQ19 because the temperature chamber is confirmed as installed.",
      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "Solid-sample clamping geometry (such as film/fiber tension clamps, rectangular torsion fixtures, or parallel plates for compression)",
        "Axial/DMA testing mode capability and normal-force range sufficient for your sample dimensions",
